vation=E2=80=9D, accusing Amazon of using its dominance to =E2=80=9Cblock i=
nnovation and make life worse for people.=E2=80=9D The startup says user cr=
edentials stay local, not on its servers, and that users, not corporations,=
 should decide what their AI can do online.

The broader issue goes beyond one lawsuit:

- Amazon=E2=80=99s view: AI agents must respect platform boundaries.
